ROS 2 Diagnostics & Evidence Capture —

Objectives
- Early detection of degradations (sensors/actuators, latencies, losses, resources).
- Automatically capture "evidence" at the right moment (logs, metrics, traces) without continuous recording.
- Facilitate operations (dashboards, alerts, runbooks) and reproduction (rosbag replay).

Tools & References
- diagnostic_updater and diagnostic_aggregator.
- References:
  - ROS 2 diagnostics (Humble): https://github.com/ros/diagnostics/tree/ros2-humble?tab=readme-ov-file
  - diagnostic_updater docs: https://docs.ros.org/en/ros2_packages/rolling/api/diagnostic_updater/index.html

Diagnostic Policy
- Each critical node exposes an Updater with tasks per subsystem (comms, sensors, actuation, compute, thermal, voltage, storage).
- Standardized states: OK, WARN (degradation), ERROR (failure). Actionable messages and synchronized timestamps.
- Update frequency should match system dynamics and requirements (configurable per subsystem).
- Hierarchical aggregation by robot/subsystem for a synthetic view.
- Design for easy reconfiguration of diagnostic parameters and thresholds.

Quality & Operations
- Rich and correlatable logs (mission IDs, tasks, components).
- Dashboards/alerts connected to diagnostic topics; runbooks for support actions.
- Use structured logging with consistent message formats and severity levels.
- Implement health checks that can be monitored by external monitoring systems.
- Capture performance metrics (latency, throughput, resource usage) for trend analysis.
